        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, thank you for referring your 85-year-old male patient, who was admitted on 02/10/1985 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination revealed prolonged expiration and diffuse expiratory wheezing. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Treatment consisted of inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. The patient responded well to treatment with improvement of symptoms and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in stable condition with adjusted inhaler regimen and oral steroid taper. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral.</div>"
            },
